\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Deere Workers to Vote on New Offer\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bob Tita \par \uc2 275 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Striking workers for \uc2 Deere & Co\uc2 . are scheduled to vote Tuesday on a contract proposal offering bigger raises and bonuses, as the farm-equipment maker tries to end its first strike in 35 years.\par \par \uc2 Deere announced a tentative deal on Saturday for a six-year contract that bumps up the raises and bonus levels from a proposal that members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  rejected three weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Workers said the earlier offer of raises and other benefits was inadequate at the same time inflation is at its highest in over a decade. More than 10,000 workers at 14 plants went on strike.\par \par \uc2 The new proposal would provide 10% raises for this year, versus the 5% to 6% increase for the first year included in the previous offer, according to a summary of the offer distributed by the union.\par \par \uc2 The briefing from the union said workers would receive 5% raises in 2023 and 2025, up from 3% increases in the previous offer. Workers would receive lump-sum bonuses amounting to 3% of their pay for 2022, 2024 and 2026, compared with 2% bonuses in the offer voted down. Employees also would receive an $8,500 bonus if the deal is ratified Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The company and union both declined to comment on the proposal.\par \par \uc2 Strikes in the heavy-equipment industry have become infrequent in the past decade, and Deere in particular has had a long run of contract negotiations without a walkout.\par \par \uc2 The strike at Deere and other companies came amid widespread labor shortages that have helped push up wages for existing employees.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211101ehb100023\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
