\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Thousands of NYC Workers To Lose Pay Under Mandate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jacob Gershman \par \uc2 184 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thousands of New York City firefighters, police officers and other municipal employees stand to lose their paychecks starting Monday for failing to comply with Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2 's Covid-19 vaccine mandate.\par \par \uc2 The exact number of city workers who could be without pay couldn't be determined. The Democratic mayor's office said about 22,800 employees remain unvaccinated and are subject to Monday's mandate. A spokesman for \uc2 Mr. de Blasio\uc2  didn't know if that figure includes employees who have been granted exemptions for religious and medical reasons or have accommodation requests pending.\par \par \uc2 Just over 90% of the city's workforce has gotten at least one shot, with thousands getting their first dose Friday and over the weekend, according to city officials. Among personnel subject to Monday's mandate, including police officers, firefighters and sanitation workers, the first-dose vaccination rate stood at 86% as of Sunday, the most recently available figure. That was up from 71% on Oct. 19, before the mayor announced his order.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211101ehb10001r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
