\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: 'RV Capital' Leads WSJ Housing Index\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicole Friedman \par \uc2 453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Small U.S. cities dominated The Wall Street Journal/Realtor.com Emerging Housing Markets Index in the third quarter, as high housing costs and remote-work opportunities drive many home buyers to seek out more living and outdoor space.\par \par \uc2 The housing boom sparked by Covid-19 has been widespread, with prices surging in major metro areas and small towns alike. While the number of home sales has moderated in recent months, demand continues to outpace the supply of homes on the market.\par \par \uc2 Many smaller metro areas around the U.S. benefited in the past year from inward migration, as residents of bigger cities took advantage of remote work to seek cheaper housing and a different lifestyle. Vacation destinations also boomed.\par \par \uc2 Elkhart, Ind., which bills itself as the RV capital of the world because its region is the country's leading manufacturer of recreational vehicles, topped the housing index this quarter, followed by Rapid City, S.D., Topeka, Kan., Raleigh, N.C., and Jefferson City, Mo.\par \par \uc2 The Elkhart area has about 206,000 residents, and the top 10 housing markets in the latest ranking have an average population size of about 330,000.\par \par \uc2 The index identifies the top metro areas for home buyers seeking an appreciating housing market and appealing lifestyle amenities.\par \par \uc2 The top-ranked markets this quarter had faster-growing populations and more interest from shoppers outside their metro areas than the market as a whole, said \uc2 Danielle Hale\uc2 , chief economist at Realtor.com. \uc2 News Corp\uc2 , parent of The Wall Street Journal, operates Realtor.com.\par \par \uc2 Unemployment in the Elkhart area stood at 3% in August, compared with 5.1% on average for the 300 metro areas included in the index. Weekly average wages in Elkhart were $1,118 in the first quarter, above the $1,049 weekly average for all the metro areas in the index.\par \par \uc2 The region's attractions include kayaking and canoeing, and an arts scene with community theaters and galleries. It also boasts both a superhero museum and an RV hall of fame.\par \par \uc2 The city of Elkhart, with a population of about 52,000, is more diverse than the broader metro area. Elkhart's population is about 26% Hispanic and 15% Black, according to census data. The median home-sale price in Elkhart County rose 12.3% in August from a year earlier to $209,900, according to the Indiana Association of Realtors.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal/Realtor.com Emerging Housing Markets Index ranks the 300 biggest metro areas in the U.S. In addition to housing-market indicators, the index incorporates economic and lifestyle data, including real-estate taxes, unemployment, wages, commute time and small-business loans.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw534\pich480\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8010\pichgoal7200
