\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: U.S. Watch\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO\par \par \uc2 Mayor, Police Union\par \par \uc2 At Odds on Vaccine\par \par \uc2 Mayor \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  and the local Fraternal Order of Police on Friday said they had filed competing motions for injunctions against each other, escalating a fight over Chicago's vaccination policy.\par \par \uc2 On Friday evening, a Cook County Judge ordered the union president to stop publicly telling members not to comply with a city policy requiring them to inform the city of their vaccination status until Oct. 25, when she scheduled a hearing on broader matters in the case.\par \par \uc2 In a filing made public early Friday, the city alleged FOP President John Catanzara was encouraging an illegal work stoppage or strike by telling members not to let the city know their vaccination status.\par \par \uc2 The union later asked a court to stop the city from enforcing its vaccination-notification requirement, saying it amounted to an unnegotiated change in the labor contract. Instead, it asked for arbitration on the matter.\par \par \uc2 The city said in August that all city workers must be vaccinated by Friday, or seek an exemption for medical or religious reasons.\par \par \uc2 The mayor says that Mr. Catanzara's effort to prevent workers from reporting their vaccine status amounts to a work stoppage or strike and that police officers aren't allowed to strike under state laws and their own contract.\par \par \uc2 -- Joe Barrett\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 Progress Made in\par \par \uc2 Containing Alisal Fire\par \par \uc2 Firefighters gained more control of the Alisal Fire burning in Santa Barbara County, as part of a Southern California highway reopened. But gusty, shifting winds could threaten further progress over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The 16,901-acre fire was 41% contained by Friday morning, fire officials said, a significant improvement from just 5% containment a day prior. The \uc2 California Highway Patrol\uc2  in Santa Barbara reopened Highway 101 in both directions on Thursday, days after the fast-moving fire jumped the coastal freeway.\par \par \uc2 Evacuation orders and warnings were still in effect Friday across the sparsely populated area where the fire was burning. Estimates from the \uc2 California Office of Emergency Services\uc2  said 230 people have evacuated their homes. Assessment teams were beginning to survey any potential damage Friday, said Kristen Allison, a public information officer with California Incident Management Team 1, which is now managing the fire.\par \par \uc2 Fire crews protected former President Ronald Reagan's 688-acre vacation home in the Santa Ynez Mountains as the blaze drew near, Ms. Allison said.\par \par \uc2 The Alisal Fire is one of several large fires burning 2.7 million acres in eight states, according to the National Interagency Fire Center.\par \par \uc2 -- Jennifer Calfas\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 SOUTHWEST\par \par \uc2 La Nina Effect Could\par \par \uc2 Worsen Drought\par \par \uc2 For the second year in a row, the weather phenomenon La Nina is expected to alter the U.S. winter. The \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2  said Americans could expect myriad conditions caused by the cooling of Pacific Ocean waters.\par \par \uc2 La Nina winters are drier and warmer across the southern third of the U.S., and cooler in the northern parts. The Pacific Northwest, the Tennessee and Ohio valleys, and some areas of the Midwest tend to see more rain and snow than average.\par \par \uc2 A La Nina this winter could have a particularly devastating effect on the Southwest if dry weather prolongs severe drought conditions that have strained the region.\par \par \uc2 The drought has prompted water cutbacks in urban areas as well as farms and ranches. It has been so acute in parts of the West that it could threaten the power supply, as water levels at Lake Mead, which help supply the hydropower at Hoover Dam, have dropped to dangerously low levels.\par \par \uc2 Past La Ninas have created significant market volatility and raised prices for many foods.\par \par \uc2 La Nina is the lesser-known counterpart to El Nino. During El Nino, the Pacific Ocean waters are warmer, and a west-to-east jet stream across the Pacific brings rain and storms to the U.S., according to \uc2 NOAA\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 -- Talal Ansari\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211016ehag0002k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
