\par\par \b \uc2 Walmart Raises Minimum Wage\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sarah Nassauer \par \uc2 401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 . will increase its minimum wage to $12 an hour and raise pay for hundreds of thousands of its U.S. store workers as a tight labor market continues to create fierce competition for staff.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  said Thursday it will give raises to more than 565,000 of its 1.6 million U.S. workers, targeting those who work at registers, in the food and household goods areas and who restock shelves.\par \par \uc2 Those workers will receive at least a $1-an-hour raise starting Sept. 25, the company said in a memo to staff, bringing \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's overall average wage to $16.40 an hour for hourly workers.\par \par \uc2 The change will raise \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's starting pay from the $11-an -hour floor \uc2 Walmart\uc2  established in 2018, a spokeswoman said. It is still below the $15-an-hour starting pay at rivals such as \uc2 Target Corp\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , the country's largest retailer by revenue, has announced a series of wage increases and bonuses for staff in stores and warehouses since last year as competition for hourly workers intensifies -- across a broad section of businesses from restaurants and retailers to amusement parks and warehouses.\par \par \uc2 Among retailers, competition is especially fierce ahead of the fall holiday shopping season when most retailers earn a significant percentage of their annual revenue.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens-Boots Alliance Inc\uc2 . said this week it will raise its starting wage for hourly employees to $15 an hour by November 2022. Pay increases will start in October and continue in phases over the next year.\par \par \uc2 The pharmacy chain said the move will cost $450 million over the next three years. This month, \uc2 CVS Health Corp\uc2 . said it would raise its minimum hourly wage to $15 an hour effective July 2022.\par \par \uc2 This week, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  said it aims to hire 20,000 more warehouse and supply-chain workers permanently. The company has also offered special bonus and pay increases to some warehouse workers to keep staff on the job and gave wage increases this year to hourly workers focused on stocking shelves and online sales.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the retailer gave wage increases to some managers.\par \par \uc2 Competitors have also raised wages over the past year. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also said this week it was seeking to hire about 55,000 people globally among its corporate and technology ranks during a recruiting event set for Sept. 15.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210903eh930001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
